      "sourceText": "| 示例 | 讲了什么 | 新出现的语法 | 为什么这样写 | 注意事项 |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| 示例 1 | 测量代码耗时 | `steady_clock::now()`、`duration_cast`、字面量 `500ms` | steady_clock 单调递增，适合计时 | 字面量需要 `using namespace std::chrono` |\n| 示例 2 | 时长单位转换 | `1s`、`100ms`、`duration_cast` | 类型自动管理单位，转换时要显式 cast | `duration_cast` 是截断，不是四舍五入 |\n| 示例 3 | 通用计时器 | `measure(function<void()>)` | 包装成一个工具函数，可重复使用 | `steady_clock` 是最佳选择 |\n| 示例 4 | 系统时间和格式化 | `system_clock::now()`、`to_time_t()`、`24h` | system_clock 可以转为日历时间 | system_clock 可能被系统时间调整影响，不用于计时 |",
      "translatedText": "| Example | What it explains | New syntax introduced | Why it is written this way | Notes |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|\n| Example 1 | Measuring code execution time | `steady_clock::now()`、`duration_cast`、literal `500ms` | steady_clock monotonically increasing, suitable for timing | The literal requires `using namespace std::chrono` |\n| Example 2 | Duration unit conversion | `1s`、`100ms`、`duration_cast` | The type automatically manages units; an explicit cast is required when converting | `duration_cast` is truncation, not rounding |\n| Example 3 | Generic timer | `measure(function<void()>)` | Wrap it into a utility function for reuse | `steady_clock` is the best choice |\n| Example 4 | System time and formatting | `system_clock::now()`、`to_time_t()`、`24h` | system_clock can be converted to calendar time | system_clock may be affected by system time adjustments and should not be used for timing |",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 286,
        "outputTokens": 170,
        "costUsd": 0.00029
      }
